From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:33:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] net: stmmac: norm_desc: Receive frames that span several
 descriptors

ndesc_init_rx_desc() limits the buffer size it programs to 2047 bytes
without the rest of the driver knowing, and ndesc_get_rx_status() drops
every frame that does not fit in one descriptor.

The RX buffer size of normal descriptors is now at most 2032 bytes, so
program it unchanged: the descriptor and dma_buf_sz agree, which
stmmac_rx() needs to put a frame together from several buffers.

Then return rx_not_ls for the descriptors of a frame before the last
one, as dwmac4 and XGMAC do, instead of dropping the frame; only the
last descriptor carries the status and the frame length. stmmac_rx_zc()
still drops such frames, as it does since commit 834ec9530832
("net: stmmac: drop split frames on AF_XDP zero-copy RX").

Such frames can now end with a buffer that holds no frame data: a type 1
RX checksum engine appends two bytes that are counted in the descriptor
but not in the length get_rx_frame_len() returns. If the last buffer
holds only one of them, "plen - len" in stmmac_rx_buf1_len() wraps and
a whole buffer of stale data would be added to the frame. Return 0 then,
and trim the frame to its length, so that the checksum byte at the end
of the buffer before is dropped as well. dwmac-sun8i has a type 2 engine;
the type 1 case is not tested.

[backport to 7.3.3: replaces the local drop-multi-descriptor-frame-tails hunk instead of
 the v7.4 834ec9530832 code; same resulting code]
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c   | 18 ++++--------------
 .../net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c
index 2cc273b..de30dfd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c
@@ -68,16 +68,9 @@ static int ndesc_get_rx_status(struct stmmac_extra_stats *x,
 	if (unlikely(rdes0 & RDES0_OWN))
 		return dma_own;
 
-	/* Frames spanning more than one descriptor are not supported with
-	 * normal descriptors: drop every descriptor of such a frame. Checking
-	 * only the last descriptor bit would hand the tail of the frame to
-	 * stmmac_rx() as if it were a complete frame.
-	 */
-	if (unlikely(!(rdes0 & RDES0_LAST_DESCRIPTOR) ||
-		     !(rdes0 & RDES0_FIRST_DESCRIPTOR))) {
-		x->rx_length++;
-		return discard_frame;
-	}
+	/* The status is only valid in the last descriptor of a frame */
+	if (!(rdes0 & RDES0_LAST_DESCRIPTOR))
+		return rx_not_ls;
 
 	if (unlikely(rdes0 & RDES0_ERROR_SUMMARY)) {
 		if (unlikely(rdes0 & RDES0_DESCRIPTOR_ERROR))
@@ -117,12 +110,9 @@ static int ndesc_get_rx_status(struct stmmac_extra_stats *x,
 static void ndesc_init_rx_desc(struct dma_desc *p, int disable_rx_ic,
 			       u8 descriptor_mode, int end, int bfsize)
 {
-	int bfsize1;
-
 	p->des0 |= cpu_to_le32(RDES0_OWN);
 
-	bfsize1 = min(bfsize, BUF_SIZE_2KiB - 1);
-	p->des1 |= cpu_to_le32(bfsize1 & RDES1_BUFFER1_SIZE_MASK);
+	p->des1 |= cpu_to_le32(bfsize & RDES1_BUFFER1_SIZE_MASK);
 
 	if (descriptor_mode == STMMAC_CHAIN_MODE)
 		ndesc_rx_set_on_chain(p, end);
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
index ec2b17c..6acfb67 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -5206,6 +5206,12 @@ static unsigned int stmmac_rx_buf1_len(struct stmmac_priv *priv,
 
 	plen = stmmac_get_rx_frame_len(priv, p, coe);
 
+	/* A type 1 checksum engine appends two bytes that the frame length
+	 * leaves out: the last buffer may only hold some of them.
+	 */
+	if (plen <= len)
+		return 0;
+
 	/* Last descriptor and not split header: buffer1 holds the remaining
 	 * bytes of the frame, up to dma_buf_sz
 	 */
@@ -5856,9 +5862,18 @@ read_again:
 		buf2_len = stmmac_rx_buf2_len(priv, p, status, len);
 		len += buf2_len;
 
-		/* ACS is disabled; strip manually. */
-		if (likely(!(status & rx_not_ls)))
+		if (likely(!(status & rx_not_ls))) {
+			/* No frame data in the last buffer: the one before may
+			 * end inside the bytes a type 1 checksum engine
+			 * appends. Trim the frame to its length.
+			 */
+			if (unlikely(!buf1_len && !buf2_len))
+				len = min_t(unsigned int, len,
+					    stmmac_get_rx_frame_len(priv, p, coe));
+
+			/* ACS is disabled; strip manually. */
 			len -= ETH_FCS_LEN;
+		}
 
 		if (!skb) {
 			unsigned int pre_len, sync_len;
